<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Duck Lake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">26 March 1885</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Rebellion</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Duck Lake was fought on 26 March 1885 near Duck Lake in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saskatchewan">Saskatchewan</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> and First Nations fighters under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabriel-dumont">Gabriel Dumont</a> defeated a force of North-West Mounted Police and volunteers led by Superintendent Leif Crozier. Twelve of the government force were killed. The clash began the armed phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Resistance</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-duck-lake.jpg" alt="Battle of Duck Lake" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Believed to be from The Canadian Pictorial &amp;amp; Illustrated War News, a souvenir number published on 1885-07-04, or ... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Duck_Lake.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
